# clangd config for libtetrisbrain — teaches the language server where
# tetrisbrain.h lives. The header sits in include/, not beside the .c files, so
# without a hint clangd floods every source/test with bogus "file not found"
# errors on #include "tetrisbrain.h". The Makefile passes -Iinclude, but clangd
# has no compile_commands database here, so it runs a generic fallback whose
# working directory is the *source file's own directory* (src/ or tests/). A
# plain -Iinclude would resolve to src/include (nonexistent); -I../include
# resolves to lib/libtetrisbrain/include for every .c under src/ and tests/ (all
# exactly one level deep). Build flags are unchanged; this only affects the
# editor.
CompileFlags:
  Add:
    - -I../include
